-A revision \(D\to D'\) preserves a face only when it supplies an explicit expansion-normalized transport from every load-bearing distinction in that face to a current node of the same grade or to an honestly weaker grade, together with its refuter. A **purpose retreat** occurs when a face has no such descendant. Its price is the lost weight
-
-\[
-\operatorname{pret}_{w}(D,D')
-=
-\sum_{p,f}
-w_{p,f}\,
-\mathbf 1[
-X_{p,f}(D)\neq\varnothing
-\land
-T_{D,D'}(X_{p,f})=\varnothing
