-Here \(T_{D,D'}(X_{p,f})=\varnothing\) means that no **total face transport** exists: losing even one load-bearing distinction or its refuter breaks preservation of that face, even when other nodes in the cell survive. A future revision may forbid purpose-retreating promotions, or may permit one only with an explicit purpose-change entry. Deleting a theorem alias after expansion has zero price. Deleting a false or overclaimed node is still mandatory; the guard requires either a valid lower-grade replacement for any surviving question or an explicit priced retreat. The table creates no inference and protects no claim from refutation.
