-### I6. Mandatory refutation programme
-
-Countermodels are not a testing programme. Every field conjecture, bridge application, capstone residue, and purpose-load-bearing creator residue therefore carries a protocol with a scheduled occasion to fail.
-
-A protocol record fixes before execution the claim and domain, seed and answer boundary, target family, repertoire, battery, frame, gauge, compared policies or architectures, W4-closed resource budget, primary observable, decision threshold, stopping rule, exclusions, and localization rule. Its recorded status is one of **UNTESTED**, **REFUTED on the declared domain**, **SURVIVED THIS CUT**, or **INCONCLUSIVE**. Survival is not support. Statistical error control may govern a finite operational decision, but it is not a probability of theory truth.
+### I5. Principal attack routes
 
-Every applicable protocol runs before the first field use of its claim, after any change to a claim-defining repertoire, battery, geometry, policy, realization map, or boundary, and at every preregistered scaling cut. An omitted or stale run means **UNTESTED**, not survived. All compared arms receive the same terminal-relevant closed resource account unless the protocol's purpose is to compare cost-to-target directly.
+This section records the theory’s main vulnerable seams without creating a revision gate.
 
-**F1, assembly–rigidity challenge. `[protocol for C1]`** Use a preregistered family of gauge-inequivalent targets, one transcript-generation rule, one repertoire accounting convention, one local edit graph, and matched construction and evaluation budgets. Measure contextual assembly distance and local delivery rigidity before examining their association. The run refutes C1 on the declared domain when the preregistered association threshold is missed or a stable reversed order appears. Repertoire changes, censoring of failed constructions, and post-outcome edit-graph changes invalidate rather than rescue the run.
+**Spark.** A5 is attacked by any genuine non-seed operative acquisition that requires direct answer insertion, identity-only adoption, unevaluated copying, or promotion by fiat. A-NJ is attacked by a system for which compatible outcomes create the theory-level support relation that Spark denies, or for which a lone anomaly itself constitutes explanatory refutation. The diagonal results are attacked by proof defects or countermodels satisfying A2–A4 while violating their conclusions.
 
-**F2, single-battery geometry–transmission challenge. `[protocol for C2]`** Split the declared reconstruction family into calibration and held-out members. Fix \(F^\circ\), its lossless transports, the local profile, the identifiability map \(\iota\), pinning order, transmission task, fidelity measure, and matched closed budgets before held-out outcomes are observed. First test C2-P1 and C2-P2 separately. Only a run passing both reaches C2. Failure of held-out pinning-order or transmission-order prediction at the preregistered threshold refutes C2 on that domain; it cannot be blamed on A5.
+**Poietic.** P3.1 is attacked by a well-formed full-code corrector whose recovery domain remains wholly inside the code region. P3.5 is attacked, on its declared routes, by an extension-ready case with no marked extension or by a marked extension lacking either route. Every worldly application is defeated when a required W0–W5 witness, package-coherence face, or identification-map distinction is absent.
 
-**F3, failure-fringe policy tournament. `[protocol for the Fertility Conjecture]`** Compare failure-fringe targeting with library-local, promotion-shy, and directionless policies using the same seed, model architecture, target stream, available operators, appraisal battery, promotion constitution, and W4-closed budget. Predeclare either delivered content at fixed cost or cost to a fixed delivered-content target as the primary measure. Stratify cases in which the fringe contains no usable localization before the result is known. Matched-budget domination by a rival on the preregistered scaling family refutes the Fertility Conjecture on that family.
+**Bridge and capstone.** B-Core is attacked by an independently identified Poietic knowledge-bearing extension for which the admissible boundary and frame family supplies no A5 realization. The finite-prefix result is inapplicable whenever any one of \(R_{P,0}\), \(R_{P,+}\), \(R_S\), or \(R_X^{\Phi}\) fails. The theorem itself is attacked only by a countermodel satisfying all displayed premises while lacking the claimed finite prefix.
 
-**F4, fixed-decoder reconstruction challenge. `[protocol for Conjecture R and E2]`** Freeze one answer-generic source-to-account decoder before exposing the scaling target family. Keep target identities, target-specific representations, later-use transports, specialist prompts, external appraisal, and hidden training examples outside the receiver boundary unless priced and declared. Test whether the receiver acquires the specified explanatory competence without receiver-owned construction and consequential appraisal. A verified fixed decoder that does so refutes Conjecture R on the declared class. A finite family cannot by itself establish or refute the unrestricted universal quantifier unless the class is exhaustively represented by a proved reduction.
+**Generator portrait.** \(R_{\mathrm{CG}}\), \(R_{\mathrm{RO}}\), \(R_\Pi\), \(R_{\mathrm{AB}}\), \(R_G\), the Fertility Conjecture, Conjecture R, and Conjecture O stand or fall by their own countercases. Their failure revises the corresponding explanatory portrait; it does not propagate through a type boundary into unrelated theorems.
 
-**F5, bounded-prophet challenge. `[protocol for residue \(R_\Pi\)]`** Fix predictor description bound, positive lead time, observation channel, system class, and adversarial environment class. For a finite environment class, enumerate it exhaustively; for an open class, preregister the generator and scaling cuts. A bounded predictor that is uniformly correct on the entire declared class while every displayed condition holds refutes \(R_\Pi\) on that class. Failure caused by a shorter lead time, extra observation channel, fixed criteria, or non-adversarial environment does not reach the residue.
+When a failure does not localize, the application has failed to establish its conclusion. Further criticism must determine which premise, map, or witness failed; no administrative rule decides that question.
 
-**F6, residue stress test. `[protocol for the finite-prefix capstone]`** Before the base step, exhibit or fail \(\operatorname{CreativeCapacity}(\mathcal K_0)\) and \(R_{P,0}\) separately. At every successor cut, separately exhibit or fail \(R_{P,+}\), \(R_S\), and \(R_X^{\Phi}\) on the accumulated predecessor cut. No residue may be inferred from the others, from Conjecture O, or from the boxed capstone. A missing witness blocks the next prefix and records exactly which residue failed; the composition theorem remains intact but inapplicable.
+### I6. Experiments are external criticisms
 
-**F7, bridge audit. `[protocol for B-Core and B-Universal]`** Select the candidate Poietic knowledge-bearing extension independently of the Spark fit. Predeclare the admissible boundary and frame family, then audit W0–W5, package coherence, the identification map, A5 no-bypass, and, where claimed, WU and A1i. A failed witness kills that realization. A case satisfying the independently identified antecedent but admitting no realization over the complete preregistered boundary/frame family refutes the corresponding field instance of B-Core or B-Universal. Global refutation requires the stronger universal counterexample, not merely failure of one convenient cut.
+An experiment may freeze a protocol before execution to prevent retrospective repair. That freeze governs the interpretation of that run only. It does not bind later revisions, reserve a permanent role for the protocol, or require the theory to preserve the protocol’s present partition.
 
-**F8, creator-purpose stress battery. `[protocol for \(R_{\mathrm{CG}}\), \(R_{\mathrm{RO}}\), \(R_{\mathrm{AB}}\), and \(R_G\)]`** F8 is one protocol slot with four separately verdict-bearing branches. A pass, failure, or omission in one branch supplies no verdict for another.
+Revision 1.3 carries one executed companion record. **F1-AR-BOOL4-001** tested the former positive assembly–rigidity conjecture on an exhaustive finite Boolean-expression domain. Its frozen preregistration, code, raw target table, verdict, and clean-process replay are kept in the companion experiment package rather than embedded in the kernel.
 
-**F8-A, characterization adequacy.** Before Spark coding, fix the domain \(\mathcal D\), the independent case predicate \(J\), positive cases, matched negative controls, and the admissible boundary-and-frame family \(\mathcal B(x)\). For a physical case, run F7 on every claimed realization. A positive case for which the complete preregistered family yields no creative-generator realization refutes the left-to-right direction of \(R_{\mathrm{CG}}\) on the domain. A negative control that satisfies every constitutive and realization face while failing \(J\) refutes the right-to-left direction. If the case selection or boundary/frame family is incomplete, a failed search is **INCONCLUSIVE**, not a refutation.
+The run exhaustively evaluated 14,451 targets. It returned Spearman \(\rho=-0.0995637588\), rigidity IQR \(0.0899621212\), and the preregistered verdict **REFUTED ON THIS DECLARED DOMAIN**. A clean-process verifier recomputed every saved target’s expression value, neighbourhood, rigidity, summary statistic, and verdict with zero discrepancies. A separately implemented full-domain verifier also re-enumerated all minimum functions through distance five, verified that the saved target set was complete under the declared recurrence, and matched every row. The positive conjecture was therefore removed rather than protected by a status label.
 
-**F8-B, role-obstruction coverage.** Fix \(\mathcal E\), the scaling family, the readout \(\Lambda\), the admissible role-fixing interventions, matched role-revisable controls, candidate obstruction environments, candidate bounds, and the exhaustion or sampling rule. First verify that the unrestricted or role-revisable histories exceed every preregistered finite scale reached by the study; otherwise the candidate is not role-separating. A valid fixed-\(r\) history exceeding its nominated \(B_r\) refutes that witness. On a finite or proved exhaustive reduction, failure to exhibit any obstruction environment for one role refutes \(R_{\mathrm{RO}}\) on the declared class. On an open class, failure to find one is **INCONCLUSIVE**.
+Other experiments may be designed for C2, Fertility, Conjecture R, \(R_\Pi\), the four finite-prefix premises, the bridge, and the creator questions. They become part of the research record only when actually frozen and run. Their absence adds no constitutional machinery and their survival would add no support coordinate.
 
-**F8-C, architectural battery coupling.** Identify the endogenous battery subsystem and its two causal uses before C2 outcomes are inspected. Intervention audits must show that the same subsystem, up to fixed lossless transport, affects both G2–G3 promotion and the C2 perturbation and matching geometry. Then run F2 with a valid \(\alpha\) and W3–W5 package under matched W4-closed budgets. A stable held-out threshold failure while every coupled antecedent survives refutes \(R_{\mathrm{AB}}\) and C2 on that domain, and strikes the one-operation reading. It cannot be charged to A5. Protocol single-battery coherence without the causal witness does not reach this branch.
+### I7. Revision note
 
-**F8-D, answer-generic jump construction.** Freeze \(G\), its seed schema, the scaling family, answer boundary, matched answer-free whole-account benchmark, cost account, stopping rule, and exactly one success mode before target outcomes. At each cut require \(G\) itself to construct \(\mathcal M_n\) and \(\alpha_n\), then audit answer-freedom, W4 cost closure, W5 boundary closure, and the preregistered threshold. One hidden specialist, invalid application witness, omitted terminal-relevant cost, leakage event, or threshold miss refutes \(R_G\) on the declared family. Failure to discover a qualifying architecture is **INCONCLUSIVE** unless the architecture class is exhaustively reduced.
-
-The raw protocol traces, preregistrations, exclusions, and failed-witness records from F1–F8 are part of the semantic event ledger whenever the system itself claims auditability. Otherwise they must remain externally available to the evaluator who makes the empirical claim.
